  "contract": [
    "Read the existing 124-byte nv_r1 class, with an ff-initialized private snapshot.",
    "Capacity-aware read returns the bytes actually written and appends no terminator; null destination or zero capacity returns0 without storage access.",
    "Stored lengths0..30 copy that many BSN bytes, clipped to capacity; lengthff fills up to21 ff bytes as stock does.",
    "Malformed lengths31..254 intentionally use the same capacity-bounded ff21 fallback instead of native unchecked copies.",
    "The native compatibility entry assumes a30-byte caller buffer. The hardware detector now calls the explicit capacity API with sizeof its30-byte buffer.",
    "Hardware cache matching, late cache changes and one-time checked publication remain unchanged for supported records."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The new bounded API and malformed/short/failure outputs are deliberate C behavior. They are not equivalence to native overflow, overread, null-pointer faults or private uninitialized bytes.",
    "The native compatibility entry still requires a30-byte destination; future legacy callers with smaller buffers must use the capacity-aware API. Resolved static REA callers do not prove all indirect callers.",
    "Direct and cached-class probes model standard copy/fill; cached-class probes execute actual size checks and critical-section control against prepared callbacks. No physical flash is exercised.",
    "The setup probe executes actual C BSN, cached hardware detection, model selection, calibration, configuration, IQS ports, registry and standard copy/fill. KV/device callbacks are modeled.",
    "An early loop-based object fell through a return under a global Unicorn memory-read observer. Restricting the observer to mutable configuration addresses lets the same original objects pass734 setup comparisons. The final bulk-copy implementation also passes with real standard memory routines; no physical fault claim is made.",
    "No final application link, physical timing, final runtime placement or device boot proof; byte identity is not required.",
    "Global sources-check still fails for pre-existing unlisted G2 resident_rom_thumb_set.S; the R1 check passes."
  ],
